  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Rainier inherited a small principality whose finances remained closely tied to the casino. He promoted tourism, property development, finance, light industry and international events, while major land-reclamation projects created space for housing and commerce. A new constitution revised Monaco’s institutions and clarified the relationship between the crown and elected bodies.\n\nHis reign also brought wider international recognition, including Monaco’s admission to the United Nations. Marriage to American actor Grace Kelly transformed the principality’s global image and supported cultural and charitable institutions. Rainier combined hereditary office with practical state development, using planning, diplomacy and selective economic diversification to preserve sovereignty within severe geographic limits. The resulting urban and institutional changes became the most durable achievement of his rule.",
